WEBVTT

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.940
Gotta get to work...

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.530
Jacket... Where's my jacket...

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.250
That one rustles when you move-koro.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.200
Oh, it's fine...

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.850
Your hair's all over the place, too-koro.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.260
Don't worry about it!

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.290
Off I go!

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.050
All right, I'll be working hard today as well!

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.230
A part-time job?!

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.520
Ichinose-san,
is your other job going well?

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.080
Yeah, I suppose so...

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.370
Glad to hear!

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:41.090
I hope you become famous soon
and get parts like Shijimi-san and Gonzaemon!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.090
Yeah...

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.090
<i>Could I really play a super popular character one day?</i>

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.800
Newbie seiyuus like Futaba-san
often have part-time jobs.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.930
Their voice work doesn't pay enough to make ends meet.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.030
Perfect.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.080
<i>Lunch break begins now.</i>

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.080
So tired!

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.500
I'm hungry!

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.450
My name is Moesaki Ichigo.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.880
However, no one here knows

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:34.470
that I'm a princess from Planet Strawberry
and a super popular seiyuu on Earth!

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.040
No matter how many times I tell him,

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:39.270
my husband always puts his underwear in the washing machine inside out.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.780
Mine does, too.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.090
And he never sorts the trash, either!

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.060
Must be nice to be so young and energetic!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.030
I-It sure is...

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.490
Kind of unfriendly, isn't she?

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.120
That's what kids these days are like.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.470
The "dreaming-free" generation?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.070
No, the "pressure-free" generation!

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.340
Unfriendly, she says?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.390
Of course I'm unfriendly.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.860
I mean, I'm trying
to stay aloof on purpose.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.470
If I became more friendly
with them than necessary...

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.600
Can you get me Polycure's autograph?!

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.060
What show are you in?

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.190
I'll be sure to watch!

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.390
My grandchild wants to be a seiyuu! Could you make some introductions?

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.490
Let's take a picture together
so I can brag to my neighbors!

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.410
No!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.330
I can't! I can't! I can't!

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.770
I'm heading out!

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.820
Good job today! Do you have seiyuu work now?

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:48.090
Oh, not today. I'm just going
to pick up a script from the agency.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.990
Why's that? Can't they just
send it to your house?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.720
Uh, it's just protocol, I guess...

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:04.020
Good morning!

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.270
G-Good morning!

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.460
These are all newbie seiyuus.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.150
At Aozora Production, Futaba's agency,

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:16.280
they all come into the office
wearing name tags

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:20.020
even if they don't have voice work,

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.120
so the managers and other seiyuus
can learn their faces and names.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.380
Ichinose-san, your script
for <i>Bodhisattvon</i> is here.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.760
Oh, thank you!

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.170
All right.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:37.800
Hm?

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.640
<i>Wow! Kamiya Hiroshi-san!</i>

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:46.030
<i>Look at the size of that stack...
He must have a ton of work, huh?</i>

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.880
<i>That's a popular seiyuu for you.</i>

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:51.650
Good morning!

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.870
K-Kamiya Hiroshi-san, in the flesh!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.060
G-Good morning!

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.950
Oh, good morning.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:09.840
Ah, Kamiya-san, the hall sent over
the gifts from the event the other day.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.340
Oh, thanks.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.840
They're over by the sofa.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.590
You also got another load of fan mail.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.650
Oh, and could you sign
the poster for a new show?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.180
It's going up by the entrance.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.280
Sure, got it.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.500
By the way, are you one of the juniors?

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.390
Y-Yes! M-My name is Ichinose Futaba!

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.860
Nice to meet you!

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.200
That T-shirt...

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:41.120
<i>Oh, shoot! I'm wearing
super lame clothes today!</i>

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.360
<i>If I had known that I'd get
to talk to Kamiya-san,</i>

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.040
<i>I wouldn't have worn
such a lame T-shirt!</i>

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.300
It's so cute!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:50.920
Huh?

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:52.910
Do you like cats?

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.460
I have a cat, too.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.360
Look.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:57.400
Look.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:58.500
Look, look.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.230
Isn't he cute?

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.470
Y-Yes!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.460
Kamiya-san, do you have a second?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.450
Oh, is it about work?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.310
Yes. Can you come
to the reception office?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.650
I wanted to talk more
about my cat, though...

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.570
Kamiya-san is really friendly, isn't he?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.280
Yeah, he is!

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:25.370
He got so many scripts and gifts, too!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.930
Kamiya-san is totally amazing, huh?

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.860
You know, you're pretty
amazing yourself, Ichinose-san.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:31.420
Huh?

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:34.370
I mean, you have work, don't you?

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.910
I'm fresh out of training school...

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.580
I'm anxious about whether
or not I'll get any roles...

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.470
I worry that people won't
even remember my name...

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.790
These girls are beginner seiyuus.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:54.150
Even though she works part-time to make a living,
they admire Futaba for having a recurring role.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:56.690
There are as many seiyuus
as there are stars in the sky,

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:56.860
but they're all in different places.
There are as many seiyuus
as there are stars in the sky,

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.150
but they're all in different places.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.360
I-I worry, too...

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.130
Let's all do our best, okay?

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:05.750
Okay!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.450
Excuse me, why are you standing
around at the entrance?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.670
This is Atsumari-san!

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.090
She's an experienced manager
at Aozora Production.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.310
Oh, sorry.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.910
Good morning.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:19.980
Morning.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.660
Oh right, Ichinose...

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.380
Yes?

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.760
Do you know Konno here?

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:28.060
Yes, she's one of the new managers...

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.770
It seems she needs a word with you.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:31.270
A word?

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.460
Do you have a moment?

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.660
Oh, hello, this is Atsumari.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.510
Thank you for calling.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.300
Yes.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.570
My name is Konno Aoi.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.360
Nice to meet you.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.110
<b>Reception Office</b>

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.020
Now, let us begin.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.040
Y-Yes, let's.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.970
The sound production
company that I work with

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.590
will be holding auditions for
the anime adaptation of this manga.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.960
Please take a look at the materials.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.090
Th-Thank you.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:08.060
I definitely think you should audition for a role in this project, Ichinose-san.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.560
What?!

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.850
Huh? An audition?

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.540
Yay!

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.110
Th-Thank you very much!

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.360
Loyal subjects!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:28.020
I'm another step closer
to realizing my ambitions!

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.120
Yay!

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.410
Ahh! Manager, uh, I was just...

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:36.300
Um, about next week's shift schedule...

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.500
Uh, right...

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.590
What? An audition?

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:45.520
Yes, I received an invitation to one.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.840
Wow, I hope you get it!

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.720
I mean, I'm sure you will!

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.080
Maybe...

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.680
I guarantee it!

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.690
It's nice of you to say
things like that, Sayo-chan, but...

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.810
Here! I made another one!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.570
Clippings of your articles, Rin-chan!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.240
Th-Thanks!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.200
And here are some cough drops!
These work really well!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.820
Thanks as always, Sayo-chan!

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:11.080
Sure! I mean, I'm Kohana Rin's first fan!

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.000
Trust me, you'll definitely get the part!

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.210
Yeah!

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:26.380
Five?
Five?
Five?

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:37.230
Total

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.210
<i>An audition...</i>

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.480
Hey, pay attention!

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.450
<i>All right!</i>

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:49.450
N-No way! If this keeps up, they'll think we're running a sweatshop!

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.470
Copehan

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:51.510
<i>An audition, huh...?</i>

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.660
What are you saying?

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.280
Our customers are the only reason we can make a living!

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:55.790
It's almost your turn. Is everything okay?

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:56.180
Our customers are the only reason we can make a living!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.070
Wake up! It's impossible
to work 365 days a year!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.420
Oh, thanks.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.960
Wake up! It's impossible
to work 365 days a year!

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.250
<i>It'll be all right. I'm sure of it!</i>

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:10.840
An audition!

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.220
We're at the same audition?!

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:32.530
Oh, good work the other day.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.130
You too.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.640
And thanks for lending us your umbrel—

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.950
Ah! Thank you-berry!

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.200
Oh, the umbrella?

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.870
Sorry, I forgot to bring it with me!

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:45.710
It's fine. I didn't expect
to see you here, anyway.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:46.010
Waiting Room
<b>AUDITION</b>

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.610
Why don't we go in for now?

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:49.710
Okay.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:53.970
What?

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.310
This many people are auditioning?

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.290
I know her!

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.530
She's the heroine of a new show...

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.090
Everyone's super popular!

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:08.620
There may be as many as twenty
or thirty seiyuus auditioning for a single role!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:13.240
No matter your experience,
you've gotta audition, fair and square-koro.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.430
Um, what role are you
auditioning for, Kohana-san?

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.490
I'm auditioning for Mimori.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.370
Oh, thank goodness...

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.010
Huh?

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:25.940
I'm auditioning for Arnadi.
I'm glad we're not after the same part.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:27.540
I'm auditioning for Isnella.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.210
But if I was up against Kohana-san,
I wouldn't have a chance.

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:33.160
That's not true at all.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.940
You think you could beat me, though?

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:35.970
Oh, no, no.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.140
We were just talking about
how amazing you were as the operator.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.630
You don't look nervous about this job, either.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:43.730
Berry!

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.030
You don't have to force yourself to stay in character now.

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.230
I'm not forcing myself!

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:51.100
By the law of Planet Strawberry,
a hundred lashes!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:54.360
Hey, we're gonna get yelled at!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.470
Ichinose Futaba-san, please come in.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.200
Okay!

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.140
Good luck!

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.400
You can do it, Futaba-san!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:09.190
Thanks!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.920
<i>I'm glad I ran into those two.
They helped me relax.</i>

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:16.570
Excuse me!

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:27.290
<i>Huh? Was this place always so wide open?</i>

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.900
<i>Why do I feel so isolated?</i>

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.280
<i>Ichinose-san, are you okay to start?</i>

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.290
<i>Y-Yes, please!</i>

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.530
Okay then, go ahead.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:44.050
There's no video during auditions,
and no one else recording with you.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:47.660
All you get are your lines printed out
on paper with no context.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:51.540
If you can't overcome this feeling
of isolation, you won't get any work-koro!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:55.860
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Production!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.010
I'm auditioning for the role of Isnella.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:02.350
<i>This character is a wild swordswoman
who brandishes a massive blade.</i>

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.030
Hey, c'mon!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.550
Quit bein' so reckless, for god's sake!

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:11.730
This is why I can't leave you alone!

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:16.390
<i>But she also has a cute,
slightly awkward feminine side...</i>

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:23.950
You know, there was actually a time when
I thought I'd live a more normal life.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.790
That's hard to believe, isn't it?

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.670
<i>She also has a burning spirit
and cares for her friends.</i>

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.460
Quit messing around!

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:40.470
What... What have I...

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:44.820
been fighting for all this time?

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:48.580
Okay, thank you.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.100
Thank you very much.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.230
<i>What?! They're yawning?</i>

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:58.320
<i>Oh, no! Did my acting
put them to sleep?!</i>

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.380
I'm Moesaki Ichigo
from Voice Entertainment!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.120
I'm auditioning for the role
of the dancer, Arnadi.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:13.590
Hey... I've been yearning
for human warmth all day...

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:16.630
Won't you stay by my side?

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.860
<i>What? They're laughing?</i>

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:24.180
<i>Actually, can you give Mimori's lines a try?</i>

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:24.760
Huh?

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:25.930
Uh, yes!

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:31.590
<i>If they're asking me to read another part,
does that mean I don't fit this character?</i>

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:37.460
<i>Oh, but maybe they think
my voice fits Mimori!</i>

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:45.530
I never expected the flowers
of Tuonella to smell so sweet...

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:50.290
I didn't think it would tickle so much to walk barefoot!

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.140
<i>He's playing with his phone!</i>

00:15:55.730 --> 00:16:00.110
I didn't think it would tickle so much to walk barefoot!

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.690
Back off!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.640
Don't lay a hand on me!

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.640
Okay, great.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.110
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.860
When do you think
they'll announce the results?

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:20.640
Next week if they're fast.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.620
Maybe in a month if they're slow.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.720
What? I'm waiting to hear back from a bunch
of auditions that were over a month ago!

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:29.030
That probably means you didn't get th—

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:37.250
How come my agency only
lets me know when I got the part?

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:40.200
They probably just don't like giving out bad news, right?

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:45.040
Still, I've had eleven straight losses
since the beginning of the year!

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:45.800
What?

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.670
Yeah!

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:51.180
I've gotta break the streak
before it reaches a dozen!

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:55.310
Otherwise, I'll just have the books
I bought for reference!

00:16:57.130 --> 00:17:00.620
I don't want to keep buying manga if I don't get a role in the anime!

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.190
It had been...

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.960
It had been two months for me...

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.970
Huh? Since you had an audition?

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.050
Yeah...

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:12.500
That's why I haven't been able
to get the hang of them...

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:18.920
Hey!

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.260
Let's cheer ourselves up
with some cake!

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.990
My agency is pretty hands-off.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:31.010
I haven't been to the office
since last month,

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.580
and sometimes I still have
to pick up my scripts myself.

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.950
I go into the office
to get my scripts, too.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.290
No, I have to get mine from
the sound production company.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:40.070
What?!

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:44.550
Whenever I go, they always
look at me like, "Who are you?"

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.040
That's pretty rough...

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.320
My teacher brings me mine.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:51.740
Teacher? From school?

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:54.640
No, my teacher from the theater troupe.

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:59.520
Oh, right. Rin-chan—er, Kohana-san,
you're part of a children's theater troupe, right?

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.810
You can just call me Rin.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.250
Lucky...

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.780
You both get the star treatment...

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:08.530
The newbies at my agency stand in the office wearing name tags,

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:11.040
but most of the time, nothing comes of it.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.760
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.100
They wear name tags?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:18.150
Yeah, they stand in a line
at the entrance of the office.

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.520
It tends to surprise people
the first time they see it.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.740
Wow...

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:26.140
People with time on their hands
just go in and greet people like that.

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:28.400
Your first time doing it
can be pretty nerve-wracking.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:33.060
Also, we record our own voice demos
and give them to the managers...

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:35.370
It's kind of rough and old-fashioned, huh?

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.300
That's great!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.880
I mean, you get to talk
to people from your agency

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.470
and get your senpai seiyuus
to remember who you are!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.350
Sounds like a nice system!

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:48.300
I see. I guess it's a good system to get yourself out there.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:51.300
It is! You should seize the opportunity!

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.380
You're right.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.650
I only have a year left, anyway...

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:57.810
A year?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:01.400
If I do my best and still don't make it past the assessment,

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.560
I'm thinking of quitting altogether.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:04.980
Assessment?

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.580
What's that about?

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:09.320
At my agency,

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:15.090
if you've worked there for two years and
don't show promise, they ask you to leave.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.700
No way...

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.540
I don't know what'll happen,

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:29.090
but I've decided to do my best
until my assessment next year!

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.600
Sorry for turning this
into a serious conversation...

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.050
You're amazing!

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:39.760
I didn't choose seiyuu work for myself,

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.910
so I don't think I've ever
thought about it that seriously.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:45.760
Don't worry about it.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.530
Yeah, you're still young, Rin-chan.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:53.370
But they'll only call you young for a few more years!

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.660
Oh, Ichigo-chan, you've turned into Evil Ichigo!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:58.370
Who're you calling Evil Ichigo?!

00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:08.280
Here. Sorry it took so long to return it.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.170
No problem.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:13.730
It's kinda lame to return it
on such a nice day, though.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.660
Evil Ichigo's back?

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.180
I said, who are you calling Evil Ichigo?!

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:18.650
Hm?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.650
It's not cute to be called "Evil"!

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.450
If you're going to add something, make it—

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:22.360
Hm..

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:26.070
I wish our three characters
got to talk to each other more.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.800
Pipo doesn't appear much, though...

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:32.090
But you have a big scene this week!

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:35.120
I wonder what'll happen to Pipo after that?

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.380
Hmm...

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.630
Good morning.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.500
Good morning.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.150
First, we've got some revisions to the script.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:55.390
Let's see... In cut 296, add a line
to the end with Pipo saying, "Pipo."

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:00.880
Does anyone have any questions?

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.290
Um...

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:04.050
Excuse me...

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:10.530
Pipo explodes, but they fix him up
so he comes back... right...?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.440
No, he dies. This is his last week.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:14.290
Huh?!

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.040
No way!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.540
What a quick exit!

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:18.920
Um, any other questions?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.210
<i>Exploded!</i>

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.240
<i>Unemployment!</i>

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.690
<i>They killed off my character!</i>

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:26.190
<i>I'm gonna be a seiyuu dropout
and a failure as a human being?!</i>

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:29.180
Pipo!

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:32.970
Pipo...

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:36.280
Please cheer up, Futaba-san.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:38.650
There's always next time...

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:39.530
Probably...

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:40.890
Y-You're right...

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:43.210
Let's go out somewhere
to celebrate your explosion!

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:44.850
Is that really something to celebrate?

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.390
Come on, there's a diner over there!

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:48.670
Let's go!

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:51.250
Wait, you girls over there!

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:51.700
Huh?

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:56.800
A-And you are...?

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.960
Will the three of you...

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.210
host a web radio show?

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.340
What?!

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.980
Web radio?!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.720
Futa-Futa, Ichigo, & Rin-Rin...

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:32.570
What a coincidence that
we were all at the same audition!

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:34.680
Right? It made me less nervous!

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:35.610
I hope we make it.

00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:37.340
Me too!

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:38.820
Oh right, about that web radio show...

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.970
I think it's starting soon.

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:40.810
Talk about a surprise.

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:42.900
That producer looked
a little sketchy, though...

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:44.240
Oh no, it's Evil Ichigo...

00:22:44.240 --> 00:22:45.560
Who're you calling evil?!

00:22:55.930 --> 00:22:57.150
Okay, we have a request!

00:22:57.150 --> 00:22:57.680
Okay!

00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:00.640
From <i>Sayonara Zetsubou Sensei</i>,
it's "I'm a Damn Twisted Human!"

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:01.980
Yay!

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:18.450
All right, let's keep going!
